Package: mixtureEM
Title: Latent Class and Profile Analysis via Mixture Modelling
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo D.", "Valencia",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "pabvalenciam@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6809-1805"))
Description: Person-centred mixture modelling for applied researchers:
    latent class analysis (LCA), latent profile analysis (LPA), and mixed
    measurement models for binary, categorical, count, and continuous
    indicators. Fitted classes can be related to external variables through
    bias-adjusted stepwise estimation — covariates via the maximum-likelihood
    correction of Vermunt (2010) <doi:10.1093/pan/mpq025> and distal outcomes
    via the 'BCH' approach, with corrected standard errors following Bakk,
    Oberski, and Vermunt (2014) <doi:10.1093/pan/mpu003>. Longitudinal
    extensions cover repeated-measures LCA, latent class growth analysis,
    growth mixture models, and latent transition analysis with mover-stayer
    and multiple-group variants. Includes model selection tools (information
    criteria, bootstrap likelihood ratio test), absolute and local fit
    diagnostics, classification diagnostics, complex survey designs, and
    full-information handling of missing data, all in base R with no
    external dependencies.
